WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.075
What changes.

2
00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:04.637
These are two different models,
not two versions of one product.

3
00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:11.013
Active Directory is a hierarchy: a forest,
domains, and nested organizational units.

4
00:00:11.013 --> 00:00:13.462
Entra ID is one flat tenant.

5
00:00:13.462 --> 00:00:17.376
Structure comes from attributes
and administrative units instead.

6
00:00:17.376 --> 00:00:21.375
In AD, much of what you are is
where you sit in the OU tree.

7
00:00:21.375 --> 00:00:25.392
In Entra ID it should be attributes
from an authoritative source,

8
00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.400
which for the workforce means HR.

9
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.338
Policy in AD is Group
Policy linked to OUs.

10
00:00:31.338 --> 00:00:36.412
In the cloud it's Conditional Access and
Intune, targeted by those attributes.

11
00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:39.685
The protocols change too: Kerberos,

12
00:00:39.685 --> 00:00:45.438
NTLM and LDAP give way to OpenID
Connect, OAuth, SAML and SCIM.

13
00:00:45.438 --> 00:00:49.105
Standing Domain Admin membership
gives way to least-privilege

14
00:00:49.105 --> 00:00:53.188
roles activated just in time through
Privileged Identity Management.

15
00:00:53.188 --> 00:00:57.651
And management moves from the
ActiveDirectory module to Microsoft Graph.

16
00:00:57.651 --> 00:00:59.850
The key idea is the bottom line.

17
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:04.087
In Active Directory, governance is
implied by where an object sits.

18
00:01:04.087 --> 00:01:07.303
In Entra ID it has to
be stated explicitly,

19
00:01:07.303 --> 00:01:10.680
as data and rules, or it
simply doesn't exist.
